🏫 School Timetable Generator
A web-based School Timetable Management and Generation System designed to help schools create, manage, and organize class timetables efficiently.
The system allows administrators to manage classes, subjects, teachers, periods, and teacher assignments, and automatically generates timetables while considering teacher and class availability.

🚀 Features
👨‍🏫 Teacher Management
* Add, edit, and delete teachers.
* Assign multiple subjects to one teacher.
* A teacher can teach different subjects to different classes.
* Automatically identify the correct teacher when a subject is assigned to a class.
* Prevent the same teacher from being assigned to two classes at the same time.
📚 Subject Management
* Add and manage school subjects.
* Assign subjects to specific classes.
* Define how many periods each subject requires per week.
* Support multiple subjects for the same teacher.
🏫 Class Management
* Create and manage classes.
* Assign subjects to individual classes.
* Generate a separate timetable for each class.
* View the complete weekly timetable.
🕐 Period Management
* Configure school working days.
* Define periods for each day.
* Set period start and end times.
* Support different numbers of periods per day.
📅 Timetable Generation
The system generates a timetable based on:
* Classes
* Teachers
* Subjects
* Required weekly periods
* Teacher availability
* Class availability
* Period availability
* Teacher-subject assignments
The system attempts to avoid:
* ❌ Teacher clashes
* ❌ Class clashes
* ❌ Duplicate subjects in the same period
* ❌ Assigning teachers to subjects they do not teach

🔄 Automatic Teacher Assignment
One of the main features is automatic teacher detection.
For example:
Teacher: Mr. Kamal
Subjects: Mathematics, Physics

Class 10A:
    Mathematics → Mr. Kamal
    Physics     → Mr. Kamal

Class 11B:
    Mathematics → Mr. Kamal
Once a teacher is assigned to a subject, the system automatically detects that teacher whenever the same subject is selected for the relevant class.
This reduces repetitive data entry and helps prevent incorrect teacher assignments.

📊 Example Timetable
Class 10A
Period	Monday	Tuesday	Wednesday	Thursday	Friday
1	Mathematics	Science	English	Mathematics	ICT
2	Physics	Mathematics	ICT	English	Science
3	English	Physics	Mathematics	Science	Mathematics
4	ICT	English	Physics	Mathematics	English
5	Science	ICT	English	Physics	Science
Each class can have its own complete Monday–Friday timetable.

🧠 Timetable Generation Logic
The basic generation process is:
1. Load classes
        ↓
2. Load subjects
        ↓
3. Load teachers
        ↓
4. Load teacher-subject assignments
        ↓
5. Load required weekly periods
        ↓
6. Create available time slots
        ↓
7. Assign subjects to slots
        ↓
8. Detect the appropriate teacher
        ↓
9. Check teacher availability
        ↓
10. Check class availability
        ↓
11. Resolve conflicts
        ↓
12. Generate timetable

🛡️ Clash Prevention
Before placing a lesson into a timetable, the system checks:
Teacher Clash
Teacher A
Monday Period 3
        ↓
Already teaching Class 10A
        ↓
Cannot teach Class 10B
Class Clash
Class 10A
Monday Period 3
        ↓
Already has Mathematics
        ↓
Cannot add another subject
Teacher-Subject Validation
Class 10A
Physics
        ↓
Find teacher who teaches Physics
        ↓
Assign available Physics teacher

